      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, adjusting risk coefficients based on cultural and social habits for District 2 is crucial for simulation accuracy. Close-knit communal living and traditional gathering practices within certain diaspora communities can elevate contact rates beyond what simple density measures suggest. These social structures can contribute to higher levels of sustained, intra-community transmission. Therefore, integrating data on these specific social networks will provide a much more nuanced and realistic transmission model.",
      "source": "target",
